<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

	<!-- The single authoritative KatLang version; see KatLangVersion.props. -->
	<Import Project="..\..\KatLangVersion.props" />

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFramework>net11.0</TargetFramework>
		<ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
		<Nullable>enable</Nullable>
		<RootNamespace>KatLang</RootNamespace>

		<PackageId>KatLang</PackageId>
		<Version>$(KatLangVersion)</Version>
		<Authors>katlangorg</Authors>
		<Company>Logics Research Centre SIA</Company>
		<Copyright>Copyright © Logics Research Centre SIA and contributors</Copyright>

		<Description>KatLang is a domain-specific programming language for calculations. This package provides the core parser, evaluator, and semantic model.</Description>
		<PackageTitle>KatLang</PackageTitle>
		<PackageTags>katlang;dsl;calculations;mathematics;physics</PackageTags>

		<PackageProjectUrl>https://katlang.org</PackageProjectUrl>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/katlangorg/katlangnet</RepositoryUrl>
		<RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>

		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE</PackageLicenseFile>

		<IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
		<SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
		<PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>

		<PackageReleaseNotes>Internal architecture repair of the evaluator's plain/counted implementation pairs; no intended KatLang language-semantics change and no public API change. The authoritative Lean model and the C# runtime now share one ownership direction: wherever a plain/counted evaluator pair is semantically equivalent, the counted implementation is canonical and the plain implementation is its value projection, so plain/counted equivalence holds by construction instead of depending on two hand-maintained bodies staying in sync. In Lean, the counted expression dispatch now matches every AST variant explicitly (the numeric/string leaves and the unary/binary operator semantics moved into counted-owned arms), the former default arm that delegated counted evaluation back to the plain evaluator is gone, plain eval is a one-line total projection of counted eval, the user/conditional/resolved/expression-position call families project their counted twins exactly as the builtin and dot-call families already did, and the ownership-first lexical lookup chain exists once (the property-carrying chain is canonical; the algorithm-returning spelling is its projection, and the formerly duplicated algorithm-returning open-lookup chain is deleted). C# mirrors that structure: the independent plain implementations of resolved-builtin dispatch (including the duplicated if/while/repeat/atoms/range switch), dot-call dispatch, the lexical receiver-injection helpers, and the user/conditional/resolved/expression-position call family are deleted in favor of one shared value-projection helper over their counted twins; the evaluator's resolve-only lexical-lookup fast path is now the projection of the canonical binding-carrying lookup; and several already-dead plain wrappers were removed. The zero-argument property cache is unaffected in behavior — its key always collapsed the plain/counted access kinds to one access shape, so entries were shared across both spellings before and after; only internal per-kind instrumentation attribution moved onto the counted kinds. The async twin architecture, run-entry preparation, budgets and accounting chokepoints, diagnostics, spans, and all public entry points are unchanged. New Lean CoreTests guard families pin projection parity for the call, total-eval, and lookup families alongside the existing builtin and dot-call guards, and the exhaustive counted match makes a future AST variant a compile-time error until it is given a counted arm.</PackageReleaseNotes>

		<Title>KatLang</Title>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="KatLang.Tests" />
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="KatLang.Benchmarks" />
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="KatLang.ParserFuzz" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
	  <None Include="..\..\LICENSE">
	    <Pack>True</Pack>
	    <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
	  </None>
	  <None Include="..\..\README.md">
	    <Pack>True</Pack>
	    <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
	  </None>
	  <None Include="..\..\NOTICE">
		<Pack>True</Pack>
		<PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
	  </None>
	  <None Include="..\..\PATENTS">
		<Pack>True</Pack>
		<PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
	  </None>
	</ItemGroup>

</Project>
